{
  "description": "Canonical corpus for the message-suppression predicate (is_suppressed / is_spam_by_classifier / is_text_blocked). Mirrors the webapp's isSpamByClassifier (decision order: disabled -> own-call DM exemption -> promoted hash -> demoted hash -> hidden topics -> hide_auto_beacons -> min_info_score) combined with the unconditional isTextBlocked half of passesBaseGuards. Messages carry the v8 axes: `tags` are the stored topics (multi-label) and `origin` is human|machine (optional, absent = unknown). Hide semantics over topics (mcmap's ANY rule): a message is hidden iff ANY of its topics is in hiddenTags; an untagged message is never hidden by topics. hideAutoBeacons hides origin machine. Preference ids retired by the classifier rework (qso, auto_beacon, bot, node, software, time) are NOT rewritten and match nothing. A policy without a hiddenTags key hides nothing; an explicit empty list hides nothing as well. Field names in policies and message are the webapp's wire names (camelCase). Canonical home is mc-chat contract/ (subtree-shared to MCProxy). Version 5: a vector may carry an optional top-level `ownCall` (the operator's callsign, SSID allowed) and its message an optional `dst`. A message whose dst base callsign (text before the first '-', upper-cased) equals ownCall's base is NEVER suppressed by the classifier half (the exemption sits right after the `enabled` check, before the promoted-hash check); blocked texts still apply unconditionally. Groups, broadcast and hashtags can never equal a callsign base, so they are unaffected. Normalisation: base = text before the first '-', surrounding whitespace trimmed, upper-cased; ownCall is normalised the same way; an empty ownCall or an absent dst never matches. Absent ownCall = no exemption.",
